# Design: live zcode contract verification

## What was verified
Built the CLI from source (zai-org/ZCode at main, node 24/tsx),
logged in through configureCodingPlanApiKey with a Z.ai coding
plan key, and ran Looper end to end on a one-task repository:
planning, worker, integrated check, publication, final review.

## Findings
- The --output-format json summary is pretty-printed across
  lines; only the stream-json result terminator is one line.
  The adapter now uses stream-json.
- --mode plan routes the plan through zcode's plan presentation
  flow; the final response is prose without the JSON. Planning
  stays in yolo with the inspection-only prompt as the limit.
  Weaker than codex read-only and claude tool restrictions; this
  is the known zcode gap.
- The zcode stack binds Unix sockets under TMPDIR. Looper's
  private per-attempt TMPDIR can exceed the socket path limit
  (about 104 characters), producing listen EINVAL. The smoke
  wrapper maps TMPDIR to a short per-attempt path. A packaged
  zcode install under a deep runtime directory will hit this;
  a shorter TMPDIR policy in resourceEnv is a candidate fix.

## Remaining
- The wrapper-level TMPDIR workaround is environmental, not an
  adapter rule. If zcode users report blocked workers with
  listen EINVAL, shorten TMPDIR in resourceEnv for all agents.
